## 5. Data Flow & Architecture Diagrams

### 5.1 High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    User([User Voice/Text]) --> UI[Frontend Chat Interface]
    UI --> IntentParser{Intent Parser}
    
    IntentParser -- "Launch App, Alarm, Math" --> NativeBridge[Capacitor Native Bridge]
    NativeBridge --> OS[Android OS Services]
    
    IntentParser -- "General Query" --> RAG[RAG & Search Engine]
    IntentParser -- "File Search" --> RAG
    
    RAG --> FileSys[Local Storage Scanner]
    FileSys --> VectorDB[(IndexedDB Vectors & Meta)]
    
    RAG --> AIWorker[[AI Web Worker Thread]]
    AIWorker --> ONNX[ONNX WebGPU Runtime]
    ONNX --> LLM[(Local LLM Model)]
    
    ONNX --> ResponseGen[Generate Response]
    ResponseGen --> UI
    UI --> TTS[Text-to-Speech Engine]
    TTS --> User
```

### 5.2 File Indexing & Search RAG Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant SE as Search Engine
    participant FS as File System
    participant EXT as Extractors (PDF/OCR)
    participant VDB as Vector DB / Index
    participant LLM as Local LLM
    
    %% Indexing Phase
    Note over SE, VDB: 1. Background Indexing Phase
    FS->>FS: Scan entire Android Root Storage
    FS->>SE: Yield File List (Text, PDFs, Images)
    SE->>EXT: Send raw bytes for unsupported formats
    EXT-->>SE: Return raw text strings
    SE->>SE: Chunk text into paragraphs
    SE->>VDB: Store Metadata + Text Chunks
    
    %% Retrieval Phase
    Note over U, LLM: 2. Active Search & Retrieval
    U->>SE: "What is my March invoice total?"
    SE->>SE: Tokenize Query ("March", "invoice", "total")
    SE->>VDB: Query matching paragraphs (BM25 or Cosine)
    VDB-->>SE: Return top 5 relevant chunks
    SE->>LLM: Prompt Context: [Chunks] + "Answer the user."
    LLM-->>U: "Your March invoice total is $3,847.50."
```

### 5.3 Error Handling & Fallback Strategy (Android 11+)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Start[Request File Read] --> CapRead[Try Filesystem.readFile]
    CapRead -- Success --> Parse[Extract Text]
    CapRead -- Failure --> GetURI[Try Filesystem.getUri]
    GetURI -- Return URI --> Convert[Capacitor.convertFileSrc]
    Convert --> Fetch[Try fetch Web URL]
    Fetch -- Success --> Parse
    Fetch -- Failure --> NameFallback[Match by Filename Only]
    NameFallback --> Display[Return Partial Search Result]
    Parse --> Display
```

---

## Summary
Building "Nice" requires a careful balance between modern Web AI (ONNX, Transformers.js) and restrictive Android Native APIs (Scoped Storage, Background Services). By keeping the ML inference inside Web Workers and building robust error catchers/fallbacks for the file system bridge, the application achieves a highly responsive, entirely private assistant experience.
